<title>BAHRAIN: Islamic Development Bank lends Senegal $24 million.</title>
<headline>Islamic Development Bank lends Senegal $24 million.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Islamic Development Bank (IDB) has approved financing facilities worth $24 million to three projects in Senegal, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank said the three projects included an agricultural project, an education training project and the purchase of 100 buses from Algeria.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-based bank -- which was set up in 1975 to help finance and promote trade exchanges between Islamic states -- said it has so far granted loans worth around $250 million to development projects in Senegal.</p>
</text>
